---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Align objects to one side of the box they cover together, or spread them so that the gaps between are equal and the outer two stay. The objects are the linked object and every --object: at least two to align, three to spread.
Each moves with what it holds. A locked object, a table cell, a mind-map node or a card in a kanban column refuses the whole call; an arrow stuck to an object follows it. It prints one line per changed object with @N and its link.

USAGE
  holst object align <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board: id, link or part of its name

FLAGS
      --object object     An object, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
      --side side         Line the objects up against this side of the box they cover together: left, center, right, top, middle or bottom; center is between left and right, middle between top and bottom
      --distribute axis   Spread the objects so that the gaps between them are equal: horizontal or vertical; use instead of --to
  -w, --workspace ws      Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
  -n, --dry-run           Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst o align "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --object e5f6a7b8 --side left
  $ holst o align "Roadmap" --object a1b2c3d4 --object e5f6a7b8 --object 9f8e7d6c --distribute horizontal -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
